 "title": "Formulas: Substituting and Solving for a Variable",
 "seo_title": "Grade 7 Formulas Worksheets with Answers (MATATAG Math 7)",
 "short_title": "Formulas",
 "domain": "Number and Algebra",
 "standard_code": "Grade 7: Number and Algebra",
 "standard_url": "https://www.deped.gov.ph/wp-content/uploads/MATATAG-Mathematics-CG-Grades1-4-and-7.pdf",
 "standard_text": "Solve one variable in terms of the other variables in a formula; solve problems involving algebraic expressions and formulas.",
 "meta_desc": "Free Grade 7 formula worksheets for the DepEd MATATAG curriculum: substituting into formulas, finding unknowns and solving a formula for one variable. 100 questions with answers.",
 "key_big": "Substitute, then calculate.",
 "key_sub": "Solve for a variable: undo the operations on both sides.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li>A <b>formula</b> is an equation that shows how quantities are related, like A = lw or d = rt.</li><li>To use a formula, substitute the known values and calculate.</li><li>To solve a formula for one variable, use the properties of equality as with any equation: from d = rt, divide both sides by t to get r = <span class='fr'><span class='fn'>d</span><span class='fd'>t</span></span>.</li><li>Undo the operations in reverse order, and do the same to the whole of both sides.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>P = 2l + 2w, solve for l</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>P − 2w = 2l</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>divide by 2</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: l = (P − 2w) ÷ 2</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Wrong letter</td><td>Match each value to its letter.</td></tr><tr><td>Wrong order</td><td>Undo + and − before × and ÷.</td></tr><tr><td>Dividing part of a side</td><td>Divide the whole side.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "What does MATATAG Math 7 ask about formulas?",
   "a": "Solve one variable in terms of the other variables in a formula, and solve problems involving algebraic expressions and formulas."
  },
  {
   "q": "What is the subject of a formula?",
   "a": "The variable on its own on one side, like A in A = lw."
  },
  {
   "q": "Why rearrange a formula?",
   "a": "To find a different quantity quickly, like time from distance and speed."
  },
  {
   "q": "Do units matter?",
   "a": "Yes. Use the same units throughout."
  }
 ],
